<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48523" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tonsĭlis</span></b> , e, adj.
		tondeo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that may be shorn</i>, <i>cut</i>, or
				<i>clipped.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">villus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 50, 76, § 203</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facilitas piceae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 10, 18, § 40</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, for tonsus, <i>shorn</i>, <i>clipped</i>, <i>cut</i>,
				<i>lopped</i>: tapetes, Matius ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 20,
				9, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nemora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 2, 6, § 13</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">buxetum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					3, 58, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
